{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"find /workspace -name AGENTS.md -print; command -v apply_patch; jq 'keys' paper_data.json; cat global_memory_summary.md; ls -la figures source_evidence; ls -la global_memory/memory.*; sed -n '1,160p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\"","aggregated_output":"/workspace/investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/vercel/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/supabase-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/data-analytics/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/zoom/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/prototype/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/investigation/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/mobile-app/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261105_100450_1793873090727309005/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/vercel/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261105_100450_1793873090727309005/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/supabase-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261105_100450_1793873090727309005/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261105_100450_1793873090727309005/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/data-analytics/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261105_100450_1793873090727309005/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/zoom/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261105_100450_1793873090727309005/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/prototype/AGENTS.md\n/workspace/task_drafting/_task_drafting/draft_20261105_100450_1793873090727309005/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/mobile-app/AGENTS.md\n[\n  \"ablation_studies\",\n  \"all_programs\",\n  \"best_any\",\n  \"best_correct\",\n  \"downstream_study\",\n  \"evidence_sources\",\n  \"final_evaluation\",\n  \"generated_at\",\n  \"grounding_sources\",\n  \"idea_titles\",\n  \"improvement_trace\",\n  \"paper_profile\",\n  \"presentation_contract\",\n  \"results_dir\",\n  \"top_programs\",\n  \"totals\"\n]\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-05 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Paired Selection Certificates with an Untouched Audit idea and matching rubric bundle. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=There are no new measured findings or evidence-backed changes to distill from this untested first-cycle proposal.\n  - evidence: Task provides MMLU-Pro and a single-GPU/API budget; no previous attempts. Supplied incumbent combined_score=0.9974625501619445 and correct=true. Its exact source path was unavailable; no scientific defect is inferred. No inference, simulations, evaluator runs, or prohibited literature access occurred. Alternatives were naive bootstrap bias subtraction, split-only reporting, and a larger adaptive optimizer. Canonical local memory is ideas/01_paired_selection_certificates_with_an_untouched_audit/memory.md; no alternate cycle-local memory path was created.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-05T21:28:48.891639+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=None, correct=False; evaluation failed: timeout; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": null, \"correct\": false}\n- 2026-11-05 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Maximal Protected Reporting Under a Frozen Prompt Bank and matching rubrics. Hypothesis: allocate n/4 to selection and 3n/4 to protected reporting for every arm count to improve reporting MSE without claiming improved selected-system accuracy. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=The allocation is an untested hypothesis and the timed-out attempt supplies no usable performance estimate from which to distill a scientific recommendation.\n  - evidence: Read task, skills, histories, manifest, campaign memory, and named prior candidate interface/source. That source documents unlabelled slots, fixed 16-prompt controls, uniform report weights, and n/4 through 3n/4 selection bounds; labels, outcome matrices, audit examples, and estimator controls are unavailable. Prior exit 124 with null score leaves timeout cause and scientific performance unknown. Alternatives considered: unsupported paired certificates/adaptive search, complex stratified rounding, and confounded prompt redesign. No scientific computation, evaluator execution, or forbidden literature access occurred. Canonical local memory is ideas/02_maximal_protected_reporting_under_a_frozen_prompt_bank/memory.md; this run created no alternate cycle-local memory target. Final status: idea_bundle_ready.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-05T23:33:43.856419+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=None, correct=False; evaluation failed: timeout; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": null, \"correct\": false}\n- 2026-11-05 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Randomized Stratum Balanced Protected Reporting and matching rubrics. Hypothesis: randomized proportional stratum quotas with quarter selection and three-quarter reporting may reduce composition-driven reporting MSE. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=This is an untested design hypothesis and the two null-score timeouts provide no evidence-backed methodological recommendation to distill.\n  - evidence: Read workflow skills, campaign memory, histories, manifest, and named prior candidate-owned source/specification. Interface supplies only unlabelled key/stratum slots and frozen-bank partition controls, not outcomes, audit data, or estimator controls. Alternatives were an unchanged quarter split, half split, confounded prompt redesign, and unsupported outcome corrections. Both prior attempts have timeout exit 124 and null scores; acceptance and scientific performance are unestablished. No scientific computation, tests, evaluator execution, or forbidden-literature access occurred. Sole local memory target is ideas/03_randomized_stratum_balanced_protected_reporting/memory.md; no alternate cycle-local target was created. Final status: idea_bundle_ready.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=clone starter; replace only partition policy; static review only\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-06T01:38:44.360839+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=None, correct=False; evaluation failed: timeout; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": null, \"correct\": false}\nfigures:\ntotal 8\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent 4096 Nov  6 05:03 .\ndrwx------ 5 agent agent 4096 Nov  6 05:03 ..\n\nsource_evidence:\ntotal 12\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent 4096 Nov  6 05:03 .\ndrwx------ 5 agent agent 4096 Nov  6 05:03 ..\ndrwx------ 4 agent agent 4096 Nov  6 05:03 downstream\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 10661 Nov  6 01:38 global_memory/memory.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 11508 Nov  6 01:38 global_memory/memory.md\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _ensure_required_fields(event: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Ensure required fields.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(event)\n    if not isinstance(normalized.get(\"timestamp\"), str) or not normalized[\"timestamp\"].strip():\n        normalized[\"timestamp\"] = utc_now()\n\n    required_string_fields = (\"step\", \"scope\", \"summary\", \"evidence\", \"next_action\")\n    for key in required_string_fields:\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing required string field: {key}\")\n        normalized[key] = value.strip()\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if value is None:\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            normalized[key] = str(value)\n        normalized[key] = normalized[key].strip() or None\n\n    metrics = normalized.get(\"metrics\")\n    if metrics is not None and not isinstance(metrics, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"metrics must be an object when present\")\n    rubrics = normalized.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if rubrics is not None and not isinstance(rubrics, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"rubrics must be an array when present\")\n    tags = normalized.get(\"tags\")\n    if tags is not None:\n        if not isinstance(tags, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"tags must be an array when present\")\n        normalized[\"tags\"] = [str(item).strip() for item in tags if str(item).strip()]\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef _markdown_entry(event: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Handle markdown entry logic for this module.\"\"\"\n    lines = [\n        f\"### {event['timestamp']} | step={event['step']} | scope={event['scope']}\",\n        f\"- summary: {event['summary']}\",\n        f\"- evidence: {event['evidence']}\",\n        f\"- next_action: {event['next_action']}\",\n    ]\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = event.get(key)\n        if isinstance(value, str) and value.strip():\n            lines.append(f\"- {key}: {value.strip()}\")\n\n    metrics = event.get(\"metrics\")\n    if isinstance(metrics, dict) and metrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- metrics: {json.dumps(metrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    rubrics = event.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if isinstance(rubrics, list) and rubrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- rubrics: {json.dumps(rubrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    tags = event.get(\"tags\")\n    if isinstance(tags, list) and tags:\n        lines.append(f\"- tags: {', '.join(str(item) for item in tags)}\")\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef _append_text(path: Path, text: str, *, header: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Safely initialize and append text to a regular file.\"\"\"\n    fd = _open_regular_for_append(path)\n    try:\n        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        size = os.fstat(fd).st_size\n        if not size:\n            _write_all(fd, header.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n        elif os.pread(fd, 1, size - 1) != b\"\\n\":\n            _write_all(fd, b\"\\n\")\n        _write_all(fd, text.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n    finally:\n        try:\n            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n        finally:\n            os.close(fd)\n\n\ndef _append_jsonl(path: Path, payload: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Append one JSON object as a JSONL record.\"\"\"\n    line = (json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\").encode(\"utf-8\")\n    fd = _open_regular_for_append(path)\n    try:\n        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        size = os.fstat(fd).st_size\n        if size and os.pread(fd, 1, size - 1) != b\"\\n\":\n            _write_all(fd, b\"\\n\")\n        _write_all(fd, line)\n    finally:\n        try:\n            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n        finally:\n            os.close(fd)\n\n\ndef _open_regular_for_append(path: Path) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Open an append target without following its parent or leaf.\"\"\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
